---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BreadcrumbNav from '../components/BreadcrumbNav.astro';
import TopicHubs from '../components/TopicHubs.astro';
import { TRUST_PAGES } from '../data/editorial';

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Editorial policy', href: TRUST_PAGES.editorialPolicy }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy — TestPrepPilot"
  description="Our editorial standards for accuracy, independence and how we research, review and correct every exam and license requirement before publishing."
>
  <div class="container | animate-on-scroll">
    <BreadcrumbNav items={breadcrumbItems} />

    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">EDITORIAL POLICY</p>
      <h1>Useful information, <em>honestly presented.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Our commitment is to the reader. We aim to be the most reliable source for credentialing requirements.</p>
    </header>

    <main class="prose">
      <section>
        <h2>Our standards</h2>
        <p>
          Every piece of content on TestPrepPilot undergoes a rigorous review process. We rely
          on primary sources — government sites, official handbooks, and direct regulatory
          guidance. We do our best to note when a requirement was last verified, as rules
          frequently change.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our writers and researchers are instructed to prioritize clarity over cleverness, and
          accuracy over everything else. The full mechanics of how a guide is researched and
          verified are documented in our <a href={TRUST_PAGES.methodology}>research
          methodology</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Expert review</h2>
        <p>
          Guides that cover a licensed profession are checked for accuracy by a professional
          who actually holds that credential. Reviewers are vetted, conflict-checked, and named
          on the page they reviewed — and they are always real, verifiable people. We never
          invent a reviewer. Read how that works on our
          <a href={TRUST_PAGES.reviewers}> Review Network</a> page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Independence</h2>
        <p>
          We participate in affiliate programs to fund our research. That relationship never
          shapes the facts on a page or a provider recommendation. A provider cannot pay to
          alter a requirement, change a ranking, or secure a recommendation. The details are in
          our <a href={TRUST_PAGES.disclosure}>Affiliate Disclosure</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we do not do</h2>
        <p>We do not accept guest posts that are disguised marketing. We do not alter facts or requirements to make a specific provider look more appealing. We do not hide the total cost or timeline of a credential to make the path seem artificially easy. We do not present unverified information as confirmed.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          When we find or are told about an error, we correct the page and refresh its
          "last reviewed" date. Substantive corrections are noted. You can report anything that
          looks off via our <a href={TRUST_PAGES.contact}>contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="cta">
        <h2>Related policies</h2>
        <p class="cta-links">
          <a href={TRUST_PAGES.methodology}>Research methodology</a>
          <a href={TRUST_PAGES.reviewers}>Review network</a>
          <a href={TRUST_PAGES.disclosure}>Affiliate disclosure</a>
          <a href={TRUST_PAGES.privacy}>Privacy policy</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <TopicHubs />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem; }

  .page-hero { padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--fs-h1); margin: 1rem 0; }
  .page-hero .lede { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted); }

  .prose section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--fs-h2); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .prose p { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: var(--fs-prose); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .prose a { color: var(--primary); font-weight: 600; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .prose strong { color: var(--primary); }

  .cta { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 2.5rem; }
  .cta-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .cta-links a { display: inline-block; padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--cream); text-decoration: none; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .cta-links a:hover { border-color: var(--primary); }
</style>
